{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["The reason for <b>after the death of the two sons of Aaron</b> is that immediately when his sons died, He warned Aaron concerning wine and strong drink, that he not die (above 10:8–9), and He further said to Moses that he should warn him lest he die in drawing near before YHWH. And it is likely that these two commandments were on the day following their death, for on that very day he was an onen (a mourner before burial), and the holy spirit does not rest amid grief (Shabbat 30), and the warning about wine — that statement was to Aaron, and on that same day this commandment was also given to Moses. But Scripture preceded with the warnings that He gave Israel, lest they die in their impurity by defiling My dwelling that is among them (Leviticus 15:31), and afterward wrote the warning to the individual. And in my opinion, the entire Torah is in order, for every place where the earlier event is delayed, Scripture will explain it there — for example, \"And YHWH spoke to Moses on Mount Sinai\" (Leviticus 25:1) in this book, and for example, \"And it came to pass on the day that Moses finished setting up the Tabernacle\" (Numbers 7:1) in the second book, and similar cases. Therefore it says here \"after the death,\" to inform that this was immediately after their death. And according to the words of our Sages (Torat Kohanim, parashah 1:3), who said: let him not die in the manner that so-and-so died — this is a stronger prod than the first. The reason for Scripture's formulation will be that HaShem said to Moses in this language, after the two sons of Aaron died in drawing near before YHWH: Say to him that he shall not come at all times into the Holy and not die."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The phrase 'the second book' (בספר השני) referring to Numbers follows Ramban's enumeration of books in the Torah; resolved as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:54:07.397846408Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}